# Default: normalise to LF in the repository, native line endings in the
# working tree. Overridden below for everything that ships inside the binary.
* text=auto

# ==============================================================================
# Files that juce_add_binary_data() compiles INTO the plugin binary must have
# identical bytes on every platform (issue #111, inheriting the lesson
# basilica-audio/Nave#48 learned on Windows CI).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Git's default `text=auto` rewrites LF to CRLF in the working
# tree on Windows. Every embedded TEXT asset is therefore one byte per line
# larger in a Windows build than in a macOS one, so the same commit ships a
# different LICENSES.md, a different manifest.json and different preset JSON
# depending on who built it.
#
# The .wav cabinets contain NUL bytes, so Git treats them as binary and never
# converts them - which is why the preset -> IR content hashes (see
# src/presets/IrReference.h) do not depend on this. But "the provenance
# embedded in the binary is the provenance in the repository" is a claim
# resources/irs/LICENSES.md makes, and without these rules it is not true on
# Windows. Caught by tests/BundledIrCurationTests.cpp's footprint assertion,
# which measures the bytes actually compiled in.
#
# `-text` means "never convert this file's line endings, in either direction",
# so the working tree gets the committed bytes verbatim everywhere. Rules here
# are LAST because git-check-attr resolves by last match.
# ==============================================================================
presets/factory/*.json -text
resources/**           -text
docs/assets/**         -text
